{"type":"text","timestamp":1794365434877,"sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","part":{"id":"prt_1c883abd2001aFYfEmVHncbAuF","messageID":"msg_1c883995c001mDPKdDshk8E6ds","sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","type":"text","text":"<think>Good, there's a pip index. Let me install flask and gunicorn into a venv in /workspace/.venv for development testing (or just install system-wide since break-system-packages is set).\n\nLet me install flask + gunicorn, and check what other packages I might need. I'll use only the Python standard library for SQLite (sqlite3) and password hashing (hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac), plus itsdangerous for tokens (already a flask dependency). Actually, I'll use `secrets` for token generation and store tokens in the DB. Simpler: generate a random token, store it in a `sessions` table with user id. That avoids signing secrets. But the spec says \"Bearer <token>\" - just needs to be valid.\n\nActually using itsdangerous with a secret key is fine too, but storing in DB allows logout/invalidations. Let me use a DB-backed token approach — simple and robust across restarts.\n\nLet me install packages first.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794365434834,"end":1794365434872}}}
