{"type":"text","timestamp":1794365877547,"sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","part":{"id":"prt_1c88a6cfa001zdQ03OXIWpFHQZ","messageID":"msg_1c88a581e0012T6Uz5J6M31YQW","sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","type":"text","text":"<think>Writing to /tmp/opencode directly is denied by the tool (it requires the parent dir to exist?). The rule says /tmp/opencode/* is allowed... but the tool denied it. Maybe because the file path doesn't exist and it tried to create in a directory that doesn't exist? Let me check if /tmp/opencode exists using bash ls (with workdir /workspace to avoid the external dir check? no, ls with the path is the issue).\n\nLet me try running bash with `ls -la /tmp/opencode` from workdir /workspace.\n\nActually earlier `pip download -d /tmp/opencode/piptest` failed with PermissionError, meaning /tmp/opencode exists but isn't writable by me (owned by root?). And mkdir failed.\n\nSo I can't write there. Let me put the test file in the workspace at /workspace/tmp_test_api.py and delete it later. Or maybe keep tests in the repo? I'll create it in the workspace temporarily and remove it at the end.\n\nLet me write it to /workspace/.tmp_test_api.py (hidden file, delete later).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794365877498,"end":1794365877514}}}
