{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794366087942,"sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"call-97ae1440-6d0a-4d48-8ead-23f02d0af6da","state":{"status":"error","input":{"todos":[{"priority":"high","content":"Set up frontend deps (Tailwind, router) and verify npm registry access","status":["completed","completed"]},{"priority":"high","content":"Implement Flask backend: SQLite schema, auth, posts API, admin toggle, static serving","status":["completed","completed"]},{"priority":"high","content":"Implement React frontend: auth, post list/filters/paging, post page, editor, admin controls","status":["in_progress","in_progress"]},{"priority":"high","content":"Build frontend and run end-to-end API verification","status":["pending","pending"]}]},"error":"The todowrite tool was called with invalid arguments: SchemaError(Expected string, got [\"completed\",\"completed\"]\n  at [\"todos\"][0][\"status\"]).\nPlease rewrite the input so it satisfies the expected schema.","time":{"start":1794366087914,"end":1794366087917}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c88da2e2001VYzBAV677VJ7V3","sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","messageID":"msg_1c88d4c56001E6iuviZWnVY3Mu"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794366087942,"sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","part":{"id":"prt_1c88da2de001eSAUrICNYT7LaZ","messageID":"msg_1c88d4c56001E6iuviZWnVY3Mu","sessionID":"ses_e377d0badffet7LSn1dj9cFwue","type":"text","text":"<think>All API checks pass. Now let me verify the admin-disabled behavior (ADMIN_PASSWORD unset → admin login disabled).\n\nLet me test that separately later. First, let me build the frontend.\n\nLet me update the todos and start on the frontend.\n\nFrontend plan:\n\n```\nfrontend/\n  index.html (update title)\n  package.json (add scripts, deps)\n  tsconfig.json, tsconfig.node.json\n  vite.config.ts (add tailwind plugin)\n  src/\n    index.css\n    main.tsx\n    App.tsx\n    api.ts\n    auth.tsx\n    types.ts\n    components/\n      Layout.tsx\n      PostCard.tsx\n      TagInput.tsx\n      Pagination.tsx\n      Notice.tsx\n    pages/\n      HomePage.tsx (list)\n      PostPage.tsx\n      EditorPage.tsx\n      LoginPage.tsx\n      RegisterPage.tsx\n      NotFoundPage.tsx\n```\n\nLet me write the code.\n\napi.ts:\n\n```ts\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"blog.token\";\n\nexport function getToken(): string | null { return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY); }\nexport function setToken(token: string | null) { ... }\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error { status: number; constructor(message, status) {...} }\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: {method?, body?, auth?} = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers: Record<string,string> = {};\n  if (options.body !== undefined) headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) headers[\"Authorization\"] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n  const response = await fetch(path, {method: options.method ?? \"GET\", headers, body: options.body !== undefined ? JSON.stringify(options.body) : undefined});\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let data: any = null;\n  if (text) { try { data = JSON.parse(text) } catch { data = text } }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const message = typeof data === \"object\" && data ? (data.error || data.message || \"Request failed\") : \"Request failed\";\n    throw new ApiError(message, response.status);\n  }\n  return data as T;\n}\n\nexport const api = {\n  register: (username, password) => request<RegisterResponse>(\"/api/auth/register\", {method:\"POST\", body:{username,password}}),\n  login: ..., logout: ..., me: ...,\n  listPosts: (params) => request<PostPage>(`/api/posts?${qs}`),\n  getPost: (id) => ...,\n  createPost: (payload) => ...,\n  updatePost: (id, payload) => ...,\n  deletePost: (id) => ...,\n  togglePost: (id) => ...,\n  hiddenPosts: () => ...,\n  tags: () => ..., authors: () => ...\n};\n```\n\ntypes.ts:\n```ts\nexport interface Post { id:number; title:string; content:string; tags:string[]; created_at:string; updated_at:string; author:string; excerpt:string; }\nexport interface PostList { items: Post[]; total:number; page:number; page_size:number; }\nexport interface User { id:number; username:string; is_admin:boolean; }\n```\n\nauth.tsx: AuthProvider with token state + user state, loads /api/auth/me on mount if a token exists.\n\n```tsx\nconst AuthContext = createContext<AuthState | null>(null);\n\nexport function AuthProvider({children}: {children: ReactNode}) {\n  const [token, setToken] = useState<string | null>(() => getToken());\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(Boolean(token));\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!token) { setUser(null); setLoading(false); return; }\n    let cancelled = false;\n    api.me().then(u => { if (!cancelled) setUser(u); }).catch(() => { if (!cancelled) { clearToken(); setUser(null); } }).finally(() => { if (!cancelled) setLoading(false); });\n    return () => { cancelled = true; };\n  }, [token]);\n\n  const signIn = async (username, password) => { const res = await api.login(...); storeToken(res.token); setToken(res.token); const u = await api.me(); setUser(u); };\n  const signUp = async (...) => { const res = await api.register(...); storeToken(res.token); setToken(res.token); setUser({id: res.id, username: res.username, is_admin: res.is_admin}); };\n  const signOut = async () => { try { await api.logout(); } catch {} clearToken(); setToken(null); setUser(null); };\n}\n```\n\nNote: after register, the response contains user fields at the top level, so I can set the user directly without calling /me.\n\nNow the pages.\n\nHomePage:\n- state: q, tag, author, page, pageSize, data, loading, error.\n- URL sync with useSearchParams so filters are shareable. That's nice: read q/tag/author/page from search params.\n- Fetch on change.\n- Search box with submit (and maybe live search on submit only).\n- Tag filter: a <select> populated from /api/tags + an \"All tags\" option. Plus, clicking a tag chip on a card sets the tag filter.\n- Author filter: a <select> from /api/authors.\n- Paging: Prev/Next and page numbers.\n\nPostCard: title link, author, date, excerpt, tags, and admin take-down button + author edit/delete buttons maybe. The spec: list shows title, author, date, excerpt, tags. Admin: take-down button on every post.\n\nI'll put the take-down button in the card for admins (and on the post page).\n\nPostPage:\n- fetch post by id\n- show title, author, date, tags, content paragraphs\n- if signed-in author: Edit link + Delete button (confirm)\n- if admin: Take down / Restore button (determine hidden state by fetching /api/admin/posts and checking membership)\n- 404 handling → \"Post not found\" message.\n\nEditorPage:\n- mode: new (/new) or edit (/posts/:id/edit)\n- fields: title, content, tags\n- tag input: type a tag, press Enter or comma to add; chips with × to remove\n- on submit → create/update; show API validation messages in a red banner\n- delete button when editing (confirm) → navigate home\n\nLoginPage / RegisterPage: forms with error messages; on success navigate to \"/\".\n\nLayout: header + nav + footer.\n\nLet me now write the Tailwind styling. I want it to look polished:\n- Background: slate-50; text slate-900.\n- Header: white with border, sticky.\n- Cards: white, rounded-xl, border, shadow-sm, hover shadow.\n- Buttons: indigo primary.\n- Inputs: rounded-lg border slate-300 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500.\n\nLet me write the files.\n\nFor date formatting: `new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString(undefined, {year:'numeric', month:'short', day:'numeric'})` plus time.\n\nLet me write index.css:\n\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n```\n\nThat's the only CSS (Tailwind's own entry file). \n\nNow, vite.config.ts needs the tailwind plugin:\n\n```ts\nimport tailwindcss from \"@tailwindcss/vite\";\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n  server: { proxy: { \"/api\": \"http://localhost:8000\" } },\n});\n```\n\ntsconfig.json for React + Vite:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": true,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": true,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\", \"vite.config.ts\"]\n}\n```\n\nHmm, including vite.config.ts in the same tsconfig requires \"types\": [\"node\"] for node types... vite.config.ts imports from 'vite' and '@vitejs/plugin-react' — with moduleResolution bundler it's fine, but `defineConfig` needs no node types. OK.\n\nActually, \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true requires `import type` for type-only imports. I'll write code accordingly.\n\nAlso `noUnusedLocals` might cause build failures for unused imports — I'll be careful.\n\nLet me add \"types\": [\"vite/client\"] for import.meta.env typing? I don't need import.meta.env. But CSS import in main.tsx (`import \"./index.css\"`) needs a declaration for TS → vite/client provides it. Let me add a `src/vite-env.d.ts` with `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />`.\n\nLet me write everything now.\n\npackage.json scripts:\n```json\n\"dev\": \"vite\",\n\"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n\"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n\"preview\": \"vite preview\"\n```\n\nNeed typescript, @types/react, @types/react-dom as devDeps. Let me install them pinned.\n\nLet me check versions: typescript latest ~5.9, @types/react ^19, @types/react-dom ^19. Let me install and pin exact.\n\nLet me do that now.</think>\n\nAll API checks pass. Now the frontend:","time":{"start":1794366087902,"end":1794366087920}}}
